A||||5||mrfiero||flywheel weight question answered!||||10||
Z||000000||mrfiero||10-05-2001||10:03 PM||||I just got my '88 GT back from the shop.....got a new clutch installed for free (well....I traded some parts, so I guess it isn't really free  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).<P>I decided on installing a new flywheel and bought a replacement one (part #10162024....thanks Paul) from gmpartsdirect.com (the original is #10162025).<P>Anyways, people have mentioned that these flywheels weigh more than the factory Fiero one and all I can say is "not true!".<P>I weighed the new one and it came in at 16.25 pounds......the original weighed (you guessed it) 16.25 pounds.  Unless there is another flywheel that people are using for '88 Fieros, there is no weight difference.  <P>The new flywheel only cost me $92.60 ($72.60 + $20 shipping), so it was definitely a worthwhile endeavor.<P>Just thought I would share my findings......hopefully I'm not offbase and confusing these flywheels with another one (some people claim the new ones are 5 pounds heavier!).||||reg||10
Z||000001||lou_dias||10-06-2001||12:58 AM||||Ok now I have 3 questions...<BR>The 88 flywheel is supposed to be heavier than the 86/87...  how heavy?<P>And the 3.4 dohc flywheel is supposed to be heavier than that.  ???<P>and what does the fieroshop's aluminum flywheel weigh?<P>what about the 3.4's in firebirds and camaros?  or did they all come with autos?<P>ok so more than 3 questions...||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||10-06-2001||01:11 AM||||The exremely rare factory tdc clutches are very strange;I would imagine that the flywheel is very different as well.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-06-2001||09:13 AM||||When getting my 3.4 pushrod engine together, I ordered a new '91 TDC 3.4 manual flywheel to use because an original 2.8 flywheel would have been cost prohibitive. It turned out that the size of both were the same but my 88's old 2.8 already had a new correct flywheel, I gave the new TDC flywheel to TerryK. I did not weigh each, but if MrFiero says it is the same, then that is enough for me.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||10-06-2001||07:39 PM||||Cooter,<P>What was the part # for the '91 TDC flywheel you bought?<P><BR>Lou,<P>I have no idea what the early Fiero V-6 flywheels weigh, but I might have one in the garage.  I'll weigh it too and see how it compares to the two I weighed.<P>||||reg||1
